# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository.
#
# Frozen experiments pin their inputs by SHA-256 over raw file BYTES:
#
#     T1/T2/T3   experiments/thermal_t1, thermal_t2, thermal_t3
#     E1/E2/E3   experiments/electrical_e1, electrical_e2, electrical_e3
#     shared     experiments/shared
#     domain     src/engcore/domains/thermal/conduction1d
#
# Those digests are what makes "T1 was not edited under T3" a checkable claim
# rather than an assertion. A byte digest cannot tell an edit apart from a
# line-ending conversion, so if Git materializes CRLF in the working tree the
# pins all break and every freeze looks violated.
#
# That is not hypothetical. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) and
# no .gitattributes, a clean clone reproduced exactly that: six T1/shared pins
# mismatched on a tree with no edits in it.
#
# The index already stores every text file as LF, so pinning the working tree
# to LF changes no committed content — it only stops the checkout from
# rewriting bytes that a digest is taken over.
#
# This must stay repository-wide rather than scoped to the pinned paths: the
# set of digest-pinned files grows with every frozen experiment, and a pin
# added under a path this file forgot would fail silently on someone else's
# machine and nowhere else.

* text=auto eol=lf
